    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d151">

                <pb facs="0461" n="411" xml:id="pg411"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Paris Peace Conf. 184.01102/229</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Professor A. C. Coolidge to the Commission to
                        Negotiate Peace</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 156</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Vienna</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-03-17">March 17, 1919</date>.<lb/>[Received March
                        19.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sirs</hi>: I have the honor to enclose herewith two
                    personal memoranda which I have received from Major Lawrence Martin. In regard
                    to the first one,<anchor n="97" xml:id="d151-f1"/> which concerns myself, I will
                    only say that as at present advised I do not share its conclusions. It is not
                    for me to judge of the second.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Archibald Cary
                    Coolidge</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d151-a1.xml" xpointer="d151-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d151-f1" n="97" xml:id="d151-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed; it proposed that Professor Coolidge be called to Paris to report in
                    person.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
